\title{A real stop at the broker whose trigger follows the market up, never down}
\description{
The stop sits at the exchange as a stop-limit, so it keeps protecting the position while UBI is down, and UBI moves its trigger with modifications as the best price improves. Give \code{trail_points} or \code{trail_percent}, not both. With \code{activate_at}, it is a trailing take-profit: nothing is placed until the last traded price reaches that level, the answer is HTTP 202 with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed}, and the stop then trails from there.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
}
